{
  "id": "tilt-aftereffect",
  "term": "tilt aftereffect",
  "definition": "The tilt aftereffect is a visual perception phenomenon in which looking at a tilted or otherwise oriented pattern for a while makes a later stimulus seem tilted the other way. It is generally described as a low-level perceptual effect, although attention and possibly working memory load can influence its strength.",
